  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Civil Society Support Room 2017-2018</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Dialogplattform f&#xf6;r syriska civila samh&#xe4;llsakt&#xf6;rer 2017-2018</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Syftet med insatsen &#xe4;r att civilsamh&#xe4;llets intressen ska tas till vara vid fredsf&#xf6;rhandlingarna i G&#xe9;neve. NOREF &#xe4;r avtalsparten.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this contribution is to support civil society to be included in the peace negotiations in Geneva.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this&#xa0;contribution is to maintain activities of the dialogue platform for Syrian Civil Society Organisations and networks to participate in the UN-facilitated peace talks for Syria. The Civil Society Support Room (CSSR) is led by the UN&apos;s Special Envoy to Syria, until 2023 with the support from two implementing partners, NOREF and Swisspeace. This contribution has supported the CSSR through NOREF from October 2017 to May 2023. The CSSR has an advising role to the Special Envoy whereby the CSSR members share their perspectives and comments which are intended to feed into the peace negotiations.

The concrete objectives as formulated for the last phase of the contribution, from 1 January 2022 to 31 May 2023, are the following: 

Outcome 1 - Participation and Ownership: Ensuring the continued inclusion of a diverse range of civil society in the political process through engagement in the CSSR and strengthening Syrian ownership of the CSSR structure.

Outcome 2 - Meaningful Engagement: Ensuring that the CSSR offers civil society actors&apos; spaces for meaningful engagement and substantive discussions, presenting ideas and recommendations that can be solicited to support the political process, including the constitution-making process.

Outcome 3 - Dialogue and Advocacy: Providing a space for dialogue and trust building among Syrian civil society actors and a platform for advocacy with key international actors.

Outcome 4 - Knowledge Generation and Management: Maintaining and developing the innovative CSSR website and online platform, with the purpose of enhancing transparency and collaboration among civil society actors. Introduction of a data analytical tool to provide better mappings and analyses.

Outcome 5 - Crosscutting Gender Mainstreaming: Ensuring that women who have received capacity building training are systematically included in all CSSR activities and considering women&apos;s interests and concerns in activity planning and thematic discussions seeking to ensure gender responsive outputs.</narrative>
  </description>
